# Deals platform: standing rules

The full spec is `docs/deals-spec.md`. It is the source of truth for data, validation and functions. The build plan and progress tracker is `docs/build-chunks.md`. Visual design comes from the supplied screenshots; do not invent new layouts.

## Never break these
- **Referral only.** No payments, no checkout. Every deal ends at an operator-owned booking destination.
- **Provider-agnostic.** All provider logic goes through the `ProviderAdapter` interface (connect, listProducts, listSessions, getAvailability, verifyDiscount, buildBookingUrl). No Rezdy-specific code outside the Rezdy adapter.
- **Server-side enforcement.** The 50% minimum discount, the 72-hour window, status changes and all auto-pause rules live in the backend. The UI may mirror them but never be the only check.
- **Status is system-owned.** Clients never set `Deal.status` or `pause_reason` directly. All changes go through the single status transition function, which writes a `DealEvent`.
- **Fail closed.** If live data can't be confirmed (stale sync, expired attestation, broken link), hide the deal.
- **Time:** store UTC, display in operator timezone (default Pacific/Auckland).
- **Money:** integer minor units (cents) + ISO 4217 code (default NZD). Never floats for money.
- **Secrets:** provider credentials only via `credentials_ref` to an encrypted store. Never log them or return them to the client.
- **Constants** (`MIN_DISCOUNT_PCT`=50, `MAX_LEAD_HOURS`=72, `MANUAL_ATTESTATION_HOURS`=12, `SYNC_STALE_MINUTES`=15, `CLICK_RECHECK`=true, `MANUAL_REVIEW_COUNT`=3) are read from one config module, never hard-coded.

## Roles
- owner: everything. manager: everything except Billing and Account. staff: read-only Inventory, read-only Business profile, own Notifications.
- Enforce on the server for every endpoint.

## Working style
- Use the project's existing stack, ORM, folder structure and test framework. Don't add new frameworks without asking.
- Every change ships with automated tests for its rules.
- After finishing a chunk from `docs/build-chunks.md`, tick it in the progress list and add one line of notes (files touched, anything deferred).
- If a change alters behaviour described in `docs/deals-spec.md`, update the spec in the same change.
